Description: Keep templates glued to a tag name in the open tag start
 A template character was appended to the tag name, so "<div{{ attributes }}>"
 had the tag name "div{{" and "<{{ tag }}>" was not a tag at all. Now:
 - "<" followed by a print template opens a tag whose name is that print;
 - a template glued to the name stays in the open tag start token, and the
   element name ends where it starts, so "<h{{ level }}>" and
   "<div{{ attributes }}>" are named "h" and "div" whatever the print
   outputs. Only whitespace, ">" or "/" ends the open tag start.
 The open tag start token carries its parts when it holds a template, and
 the name is taken from those parts, keeping template text verbatim and
 lower-casing only the HTML around it.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("Twig as part of the markup structure")
